# Example: Arize Phoenix observability integration
#
# Sends OpenTelemetry traces from LiteLLM to a self-hosted Phoenix instance.
# Phoenix accepts OTLP traces on port 6006 (HTTP) at /v1/traces.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Merge the litellm_settings and environment_variables sections below
#      into your config.yaml.
#   2. Redeploy:  terraform destroy -auto-approve && terraform apply -auto-approve
#   3. Send a request through LiteLLM and verify traces appear in the Phoenix UI.
#
# Phoenix UI: http://phoenix.service.consul:<port>  (or via Traefik)
# Docs: https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/observability/phoenix_integration

# Add to litellm_settings:
litellm_settings:
  callbacks: ["arize_phoenix"]

# The PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_HTTP_ENDPOINT env var is set automatically by
# the Nomad job template using Consul service discovery, so no manual
# endpoint configuration is needed. See litellm.nomad.hcl for details.
